This directory contains files extracted from the Intel FreeBSD ice
driver. This uses the FreeBSD main branch, git SHA
310145642312e1c5fb3d8efa8321cf905d0354c4.

These files are the OS-independent "common code". OS adaptation lives in
the ../ice_osdep.h and ../ice_osdep.c shim and in the surrounding driver.
Local validation changes in this directory are marked with "illumos:"
comments; a future import must retain or replace those guards.

The following files were imported but are intentionally not compiled (see
the ICE_INTC_OBJS list in usr/src/uts/common/Makefile.files):

    ice_dcb.c		DCB/LLDP support; no coupling into the rest of the
			common code, omitted until needed.
    ice_vf_mbx.c	SR-IOV virtchnl mailbox; omitted until IOV support
			is added.

The following illumos changes have further modified the common code:

    Response count/size guards in ice_common.c, ice_switch.c,
    ice_ddp_common.c, and ice_sched.c, plus bounded debug name printing.
    Scheduler resource admission accepts only ICE_SCHED_5_LAYERS or
    ICE_SCHED_9_LAYERS and requires nonzero sibling-group sizes for every
    layer used as a child fanout. Validation precedes publishing scheduler
    state. See usr/src/test/ice-tests/sched_resources.py for the executable
    query-boundary regression and core_counts.py for the guard inventory.
